1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
2,027 hours of work a year.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,000
By the time we leave, it's long been dark.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,567
This is the Ministry of Labor's figure:

4
00:00:05,567 --> 00:00:07,700
total annual working hours for 2025.

5
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,900
At eight hours a day,

6
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:11,100
that is 253 working days.

7
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:12,433
In 2014 it was longer:

8
00:00:12,433 --> 00:00:14,333
2,135 hours.

9
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:15,233
Then it kept falling.

10
00:00:15,233 --> 00:00:16,867
In the pandemic year it dipped below 2,000.

11
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:18,100
Then it climbed again.

12
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,100
Last year brought more holidays,

13
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,433
yet hours fell by just 3.6.

14
00:00:21,433 --> 00:00:22,767
Why won't it come down?

15
00:00:22,767 --> 00:00:24,300
Nearly all of us work full time.

16
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,267
Part-timers are only 3 to 4 percent here.

17
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:28,067
In Japan, about one in four.

18
00:00:28,067 --> 00:00:29,267
Then there is overtime.

19
00:00:29,267 --> 00:00:30,833
Regular hours fell last year,

20
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:32,167
but overtime rose.

21
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:33,467
And then there is after work.

22
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:34,500
One in four

23
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,600
got a message assigning them work.

24
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,300
But this number needs careful reading.

25
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,233
Full-time and part-time workers

26
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:40,400
are averaged together.

27
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,333
So we can't simply say

28
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:42,167
that we work nearly

29
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:44,367
400 hours more than people in Japan.

30
00:00:44,367 --> 00:00:46,400
Looking at full-timers only,

31
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,400
Taiwan's week is 41.5 hours,

32
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,667
shorter than Japan's.

33
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:50,700
Next time: rent.
